  m_Name: Blade2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Rear Blade Shroud Left
  description: The Rear Blade Shroud Left is a ring-like component that surrounds
    the Rear Blade Left, providing a seal between the blade and the engine casing
    to prevent gas leaks and maintain pressure. Made from a high-temperature resistant
    material, it is designed to withstand the extreme conditions found at the rear
    of the engine. One interesting detail is that the shroud is often segmented to
    allow for thermal expansion and contraction.
